ZN504XG-D voice Path B: bring up the Le9643 SLIC over PCM1 + ZSI.

Self-contained replacement for the removed Path A dts patches
(201-04 sound-slic / 201-05 afe-reset): the airoha_voip PCM/ZSI driver
stack:

  pcm0  airoha,en7581-pcm  @ 0x1fbd0000, GIC_SPI 27, EN7581_PCM1_RST,
        naoki66's validated EN7581 interface-control value 0xf5051306
  zsi0  airoha,en7581-zsi  @ 0x1fbd1000, EN7523_CLK_SLIC clock,
        EN7581_PCM1_ZSI_ISI_RST reset
  slic0 microsemi,le9643   one FXS line at bus slot 4 (DMA channel 0)

The SoC dtsi keeps both sound and afe nodes status="disabled" by
default, so no explicit disabling is needed once 201-04/201-05 are gone.

Pin hypothesis: SLIC routed to the pcm_spi group (GPIO18-25) +
pcm_spi_cs1 (GPIO43), the layout naoki66 validated on the XG2010G (same
SoC).  Caveat: GPIO18/19/20/24 also drive the PON/LOS/Internet/phone
LEDs, so the pinmux claim may conflict with leds-gpio by probe order.
If the SLIC does not answer on the ZSI bus at runtime, retry the pcm1
group (GPIO22-25, only the phone LED overlaps) before assuming a wiring
fault.

Companion driver patch: voice/airoha-voip/patches/001-en7581-support.patch
adds the en7581 compatibles to the pcm/zsi/le9642 drivers.

Signed-off-by: ZN504XG-D voice porting project
diff --git a/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-znxt-zn50xg-d-common.dtsi b/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-znxt-zn50xg-d-common.dtsi
index 9c3005d..485d50e 100644
--- a/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-znxt-zn50xg-d-common.dtsi
+++ b/target/linux/airoha/dts/an7581-znxt-zn50xg-d-common.dtsi
@@ -110,6 +110,87 @@
 		regulator-max-microvolt = <3300000>;
 		regulator-name = "fixed-3.3V";
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * Voice stack (Path B): Microsemi Le9643 SLIC on the PCM1 engine with
+	 * the ZSI transport, per the airoha_voip driver stack.  Replaces the
+	 * abandoned AFE/ASoC route (dts-patches/201-04 and 201-05, removed);
+	 * the SoC dtsi keeps both sound and afe nodes disabled by default.
+	 *
+	 * Pin hypothesis: the SLIC digital lines are routed to the pcm_spi
+	 * group (GPIO18-25) plus chip select pcm_spi_cs1 (GPIO43), the same
+	 * layout naoki66 validated on the XG2010G (AN7581).  Caveat: GPIO18/19/
+	 * 20/24 drive the PON/LOS/Internet/phone LEDs, so the pinmux claim can
+	 * conflict with leds-gpio depending on probe order.  If the SLIC does
+	 * not answer on the ZSI bus at runtime, retry with the pcm1 group
+	 * (GPIO22-25, only GPIO24/phone LED overlaps) before assuming a
+	 * wiring fault.
+	 *
+	 * IRQ and register layout follow the vendor map naoki66 uses on the
+	 * XG2010G: PCM at 0x1fbd0000, ZSI wrapper at +0x1000, GIC SPI 27.
+	 */
+	pcm0: pcm@1fbd0000 {
+		compatible = "airoha,en7581-pcm";
+		reg = <0x0 0x1fbd0000 0x0 0x1000>;
+		reg-names = "pcm";
+
+		interrupts = <GIC_SPI 27 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+
+		resets = <&scuclk EN7581_PCM1_RST>;
+		reset-names = "pcm";
+
+		/* naoki66's validated EN7581 interface-control value. */
+		airoha,pcm-interface-control = <0xf5051306>;
+
+		airoha,tx-slot-config = <0x10101000 0x10301020
+					 0x10501040 0x10701060>;
+		airoha,rx-slot-config = <0x10101000 0x10301020
+					 0x10501040 0x10701060>;
+		airoha,dma-channel-mask = <0x01>;
+
+		status = "okay";
+	};
+
+	zsi0: zsi@1fbd1000 {
+		compatible = "airoha,en7581-zsi";
+		reg = <0x0 0x1fbd1000 0x0 0x1000>;
+		reg-names = "zsi";
+
+		clocks = <&scuclk EN7523_CLK_SLIC>;
+		clock-names = "slic";
+		resets = <&scuclk EN7581_PCM1_ZSI_ISI_RST>;
+		reset-names = "zsi";
+
+		/*
+		 * Only zsi0 claims the pins: muxing the same group from pcm0
+		 * as well would just earn a second -EBUSY style warning from
+		 * the pinmux core, the mux result is identical.
+		 */
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&pcm_spi_pins>, <&pcm_spi_cs1_pins>;
+
+		#address-cells = <1>;
+		#size-cells = <0>;
+
+		airoha,zsi-gap-us = <5000>;
+
+		status = "okay";
+
+		slic0: slic@0 {
+			compatible = "microsemi,le9643";
+			reg = <0>;
+
+			airoha,zsi = <&zsi0>;
+			airoha,pcm = <&pcm0>;
+			airoha,lines = <1>;
+
+			/* Single FXS line; bus slot 4 = DMA channel 0 with the
+			 * default timeslot table above. */
+			airoha,bus-slots = <4>;
+
+			status = "okay";
+		};
+	};
 };
 
 &en7581_pinctrl {
@@ -150,4 +231,18 @@
 			pins = "gpio46";
 		};
 	};
+	/* PCM bus plus the ZSI-multiplexed SLIC control channel and CS1. */
+	pcm_spi_pins: pcm-spi-pins {
+		mux {
+			function = "pcm_spi";
+			groups = "pcm_spi";
+		};
+	};
+
+	pcm_spi_cs1_pins: pcm-spi-cs1-pins {
+		mux {
+			function = "pcm_spi";
+			groups = "pcm_spi_cs1";
+		};
+	};
 };
 
